WEBVTT

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:05.150
Hey, Shingetsu! Hey!

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:07.480
<i>Hurry! Please hurry, Yuma!</i>

00:00:09.370 --> 00:00:10.320
Shingetsu!

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.610
Just sit tight!

00:00:16.360 --> 00:00:17.670
Th-That's...!

00:00:20.890 --> 00:00:21.650
Shingetsu!

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:25.000
You made it, Officer Yuma!

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.920
Yeah. But... who's he?

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.590
We've got some interference.
 This match is postponed, I suppose.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:36.680
Wait, Vector!

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:42.830
Shingetsu!

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:46.060
Shingetsu...! Hey, are you okay?!

00:00:46.530 --> 00:00:46.970
Hey!

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:48.070
Yeah...

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:49.980
Just who was that guy?

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:55.830
He's the most atrocious Barian 
who's been with us for a long time...

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.490
It's Vector!

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.160
Vector?

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:04.000
Officer Yuma, I'm going to chase after him.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:07.620
I'm counting on you to keep the peace in this world in my absence!

00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:10.960
Yes, Inspector Shingetsu!

00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:14.650
I'm lending you these cards.

00:01:15.440 --> 00:01:15.870
Eh?

00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:18.600
I'm sure they'll be of some help to you.

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:22.830
Five of them? Are these Barian cards?

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:30.480
I'm sure you know this, but you need to keep these cards a secret from Astral. Understand?

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:34.690
Y-Yeah... But Shingetsu...

00:01:34.690 --> 00:01:37.400
Isn't it time to reveal this to Astral?

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.910
We can't!

00:01:38.910 --> 00:01:41.310
If my identity is exposed right now,

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:44.500
Astral will be placed in grave danger!

00:01:46.120 --> 00:01:46.960
Astral...

00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:49.920
I'll tell him the truth sooner or later for sure.

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.130
Until then, you need to believe in me!

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.300
I understand, Inspector Shingetsu!

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.330
I'm counting on you, Officer Yuma!

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.460
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:02:12.460 --> 00:02:18.430
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:21.140
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:02:30.940 --> 00:02:33.490
<i>Preparations for the fight are ready</i>

00:02:33.490 --> 00:02:36.570
<i>I can already hear the shivering of my heart</i>

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:41.080
<i>Been waiting this whole time</i>

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:43.450
<i>I may meet with defeat...</i>

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.670
<i>But that's exactly why I have to stand back up</i>

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:51.210
<i>Need to get stronger again</i>

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.340
<i>It's good to believe</i>

00:02:53.510 --> 00:02:56.050
<i>The "now", more than ever before, is</i>

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:58.510
<i>but another limit to break down</i>

00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:01.560
<i>I can cross with ease</i>

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:04.020
<i>It's just beginning now</i>

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:10.060
<i>This story continues to be etched into my heart endlessly</i>

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:12.820
<i>These feelings... burning up inside!</i>

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:14.280
<i>Right here in my hand,</i>

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.990
<i>I'm holding a powerful trump card.</i>

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:28.040
<i>With an unbreakable heart, I face toward my dream!</i>

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:42.160
After falling to Yuma Tsukumo,

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:46.580
Alit and Gilag suffered major injuries in the Human World.

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:48.370
They still haven't woken up even now.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:53.120
Misael, now that it's come to this, the two of us will have to settle this ourselves.

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:54.250
"Shingetsu's Crisis! The Attack of Vector the Manipulator!"

00:03:55.710 --> 00:03:57.130
What's <i>wrong</i>?!

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.720
Trying to imitate the feeling of
 repentance through these gloomy times?!

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:07.050
Good 'ol Vector the Great'll lend you an ear!

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:08.850
You're...!

00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:10.480
Vector!

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:16.190
<i>Ah</i>, they're a <i>total mess</i>!

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:19.360
This is what happens when you let 
<i>powerless scrubs</i> do the work!

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.530
You beggin' for forgiveness?!

00:04:23.910 --> 00:04:25.200
Then I'll <i>forgive you</i>!

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.040
Stop it, Misael.

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:39.380
Now is not the time for us to be fighting each other.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:40.880
I won't stop next time.

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:43.170
Why <i>thank you</i>.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.140
Vector, as always, you show up on a whim.

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:50.770
You used Dr. Faker and Tron

00:04:50.770 --> 00:04:53.310
to carry out your plan to destroy the Astral Word.

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.400
But that was prevented by Yuma and Astral.

00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:03.110
You didn't even take responsibility for your failure.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:05.240
Where did you disappear to?

00:05:06.530 --> 00:05:09.700
It wasn't a <i>failure</i>! This was all part of my plan!

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.540
Yuma. Astral. Kaito. Ryouga.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:19.670
It was all so I could beat the four of them to a pulp and put an end to this fight!

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.460
A grand victory within thousands of failures!

00:05:23.090 --> 00:05:26.930
You two can wager this entire affair on <i>my hands</i>!

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:28.970
No one wants to hear your plan!

00:05:28.970 --> 00:05:29.640
Understood.

00:05:30.470 --> 00:05:33.890
However, you will not act on your own accord again.

00:05:33.890 --> 00:05:37.440
If you do something like that again, I will...

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:40.690
Now!

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.030
It's for the worst if we don't begin right now!

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:52.870
As long as I have these cards Shingetsu gave me and Hope Ray V...

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:54.580
I'm practically invincible!

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.120
Heck yeah! I should take these cards and go on Barian cleanup!

00:05:58.120 --> 00:05:59.630
Why are you so high in spirits?

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:00.840
Kotori!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.500
Keeping secrets from us!

00:06:03.130 --> 00:06:05.090
Why are you standing around up here for?

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:07.300
To summarize, Yuma-<i>kun</i> is...

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:09.720
...unable to hide things from us, or not!

00:06:15.140 --> 00:06:17.690
Hey! Get out here!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:21.400
Is a Barian here, or not at all?!

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.440
Any Barian showing itself'll 
get a good beating from this cat, meow!

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.990
Man... Why do these guys need to be here just for my patrol?

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:32.580
They just want to help you out, Yuma.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.870
Listen, you!

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.450
What is that thing?

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.840
Wh-What the heck is that?

00:06:59.850 --> 00:07:02.270
Kotori! You all okay?!

00:07:02.940 --> 00:07:03.610
Yeah...

00:07:03.610 --> 00:07:04.770
I'm okay, or not.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:08.990
What's going on, Yuma?

00:07:09.240 --> 00:07:10.740
Yeah, well...

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:16.740
You're...!

00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.330
My name is Vector.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:23.630
Barian's <i>strongest warrior</i>!

00:07:24.290 --> 00:07:25.590
That Vector guy!

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:32.550
<i>He's the most atrocious Barian 
who's been with us for a long time...</i>

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:34.470
<i>It's Vector!</i>

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.520
Yuma Tsukumo! Astral!

00:07:37.680 --> 00:07:41.690
I came here to rip this world apart,
 and you two <i>along with it</i>!

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:42.900
What'd you say?!

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:43.900
Yuma, the guys!

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:44.860
Yeah!

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:46.070
Everyone, run away!

00:07:46.070 --> 00:07:46.690
Yeah!

00:07:48.690 --> 00:07:51.700
Barian's Sphere Field, expand!

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:04.920
Yuma!

00:08:10.630 --> 00:08:13.380
It's been <i>so long</i> since our last Duel together!

00:08:13.380 --> 00:08:16.850
"So long" my behind!
 I don't even know who you ar-

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:19.060
Did you <i>forget already</i>?!

00:08:19.770 --> 00:08:22.770
I stole Dr. Faker's body

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:26.860
and had that <i>exhilarating</i> Duel with you guys!

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:30.480
So you're the one who manipulated Dr. Faker...

00:08:30.530 --> 00:08:32.030
One of the Barians?

00:08:32.030 --> 00:08:34.990
I'm <i>so honored</i> you <i>remember me</i>!

00:08:34.990 --> 00:08:38.990
I'll smash <i>everything</i> to <i>rubble</i>!

00:08:39.580 --> 00:08:43.960
And not just the <i>Astral World</i>!
 That includes <i>this world</i> and <i>everything</i>!

00:08:43.960 --> 00:08:45.210
What?!

00:08:45.210 --> 00:08:46.670
Even this world...?

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.880
Stop joking! I'm not gonna let you do as you please!

00:08:51.590 --> 00:08:53.340
Duel Disk, set!

00:08:58.470 --> 00:09:00.140
D-Gazer, set!

00:09:02.850 --> 00:09:06.520
Now, it's for the worst if we don't get started!

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:08.770
Duel!!

00:09:09.570 --> 00:09:11.610
<i>I'll</i> take the first turn!

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.900
My turn! Draw!

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:18.200
I Summon Umbral Ghoul!

00:09:25.330 --> 00:09:28.630
And then I activate Umbral Ghoul's effect!

00:09:29.210 --> 00:09:32.130
I can make this Monster's Attack Power zero

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:37.680
in order to Special Summon an Umbral Monster with zero Attack Points from my hand!

00:09:38.090 --> 00:09:39.970
Come, Umbral Unform!

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.720
He's about to do it, Yuma!

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:47.350
I Overlay the Level Four Umbral Ghoul and Umbral Unform!

00:09:48.400 --> 00:09:51.900
I use these two Monsters to build the Overlay Network!

00:09:52.530 --> 00:09:54.150
Xyz Summon!

00:09:57.150 --> 00:09:59.280
Number 66!

00:10:06.250 --> 00:10:09.670
Dominant Stag Beetle - Master Key Beetle!

00:10:12.960 --> 00:10:14.800
He played a Number right at the start!

00:10:15.800 --> 00:10:17.720
Master Key Beetle...

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:23.810
<i>Then</i> I activate the Continuous Magic, 
Magical Sealing Coffin!

00:10:24.220 --> 00:10:28.230
This card allows me to choose one card from my opponent's deck,

00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:29.810
and seal it up!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:30.440
What?!

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:33.940
Yuma Tsukumo...

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:37.740
I'm well aware that you're holding one of our Barian cards...

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:45.950
I will seal away the Limited Barian's Force card you own!

00:10:52.840 --> 00:10:54.550
Limited Barian's Force was...!

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:02.390
Our Rank-Up was sealed away?!

00:11:02.600 --> 00:11:04.350
Now Hope Ray V is...

00:11:04.810 --> 00:11:08.350
Now here I go! I activate Master Key Beetle's effect!

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:13.230
I can detach one Overlay Unit to select one card on the field,

00:11:13.520 --> 00:11:16.570
and protect that card against any effect that destroys cards!

00:11:19.570 --> 00:11:22.160
I select Magical Sealing Coffin!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.830
He's got Limited Barian's Force locked up so tightly!

00:11:26.950 --> 00:11:30.870
Does that mean he's that afraid of that card's power?

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.840
I set one card face-down and end my turn!

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:40.090
Without that card, you two stand no <i>chance</i> of winning!

00:11:41.880 --> 00:11:43.890
Yuma...

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:51.390
C'mon, what's <i>wrong</i>? Come at me already!

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:53.730
My turn! Draw!

00:11:55.940 --> 00:11:58.070
I Summon Gagaga Magician!

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:06.160
Then I activate the Magic Card, Gagaga Wind!

00:12:06.490 --> 00:12:11.540
I can Special Summon a Gagaga Monster from my hand and raise its level by one!

00:12:11.540 --> 00:12:13.290
Come, Gagaga Girl!

00:12:20.630 --> 00:12:22.130
Here Yuma goes!

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:23.180
He's about to purr!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:25.050
Go, Yuma!

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:30.220
I Overlay the Level Four Gagaga Magician and Gagaga Girl!

00:12:31.020 --> 00:12:33.980
I build the Overlay Network using these two Monsters!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:35.770
Xyz Summon!

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:42.190
Come forth, Number 39! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:49.290
Hope without your Rank-Up Magic?!

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:52.710
Is this what they call "hoping for evolution"?!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:56.630
Yuma, use Gagaga Girl's effect!

00:12:56.920 --> 00:12:57.330
Right!

00:12:57.790 --> 00:13:01.300
I activate the Xyz Material Gagaga Girl's effect!

00:13:01.760 --> 00:13:04.090
She makes the Attack Power of an opponent's Monster zero!

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:05.470
Zero Zero Call!

00:13:07.800 --> 00:13:10.850
What?! Master Key Beetle's Attack Power...?!

00:13:11.350 --> 00:13:15.600
Go, Hope! Beat Master Key Beetle down!

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.110
Hope Sword Slash!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.330
I activate Master Key Beetle's effect!

00:13:31.790 --> 00:13:35.620
By using sending the card this Monster used its effect on to the Graveyard,

00:13:35.790 --> 00:13:38.290
I can negate Master Key Beetle's destruction!

00:13:38.920 --> 00:13:41.800
I break the Magical Sealing Coffin!

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:48.050
And be reborn, Master Key Beetle!

00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.220
The card that was sealed

00:13:54.220 --> 00:13:56.600
returns to your hand during this turn.

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.520
Heck yeah! Now I got my card back!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:00.610
<i>Strange...</i>

00:14:01.520 --> 00:14:05.440
<i>He let go of Limited Barian's Force this easily?</i>

00:14:06.240 --> 00:14:10.820
Trap, activate! Key of Guilt - Sin Key Law!

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:15.000
This card can be activated when a Monster I control isn't destroyed in battle,

00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:18.170
and it Special Summons three Umbral Mirage Tokens!

00:14:19.750 --> 00:14:21.380
Wh-What are those?

00:14:22.040 --> 00:14:22.670
Those are...

00:14:23.960 --> 00:14:26.010
The Attack Power of these tokens...

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:31.050
are equal to the Attack Power of the Monster that wasn't destroyed, Master Key Beetle!

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:33.100
Then they have zero Attack Points!

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.970
No, it's him we're talking about...

00:14:35.890 --> 00:14:37.770
He must be planning something.

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:41.110
I'll end my turn there!

00:14:41.610 --> 00:14:45.570
And Limited Barian's Force returns to my hand!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:48.070
Yes! As long as I have this card...

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:51.120
Don't lose focus, Yuma. Here he comes.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.620
Time to enjoy myself.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:57.870
My turn! Draw!

00:14:58.660 --> 00:15:02.960
I activate the Magic Card, Umbral Refresh, from my hand!

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:08.630
It returns the Attack Power of a Monster that had its Attack Power lowered back to normal!

00:15:08.630 --> 00:15:12.340
It brings Master Key Beetle's Attack Power back to 2500!

00:15:13.260 --> 00:15:18.390
And I gain that amount as my Life Points!

00:15:19.560 --> 00:15:21.730
Wh-What the heck is <i>with</i> that?!

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:25.860
And then, the Attack Points of the three Umbral Mirage Tokens

00:15:25.860 --> 00:15:28.900
become equal to Master Key Beetle's become 2500!

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:32.360
Four Monsters with 2500 Attack Points?!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:39.620
I attack Aspiring Emperor - Hope
 with two of the Umbral Mirage Tokens!

00:15:42.000 --> 00:15:45.170
Hmph! Hope's Attack Power is also 2500 like theirs!

00:15:45.590 --> 00:15:49.170
And Numbers can only be destroyed by other Numbers!

00:15:50.170 --> 00:15:52.380
Yuma, protect yourself against this attack!

00:15:52.470 --> 00:15:52.840
What?!

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:55.350
He has to be aiming for something!

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:56.760
G-Got it.

00:15:57.600 --> 00:16:00.100
I detach two Overlay Units

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.020
in order to negate both Monsters' attacks!

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:05.400
Moon Barrier!

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:11.900
There's still the third Umbral Mirage Token! Go!

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:14.700
Just what is this guy...?

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:16.280
He can't be...!

00:16:16.990 --> 00:16:19.370
Attack Spiring Emperor - Hope!

00:16:24.830 --> 00:16:28.460
This moment, I activate the Quick-Play Magic, Umbral Death Blood!

00:16:31.170 --> 00:16:34.640
When one Umbral Monster is destroyed,

00:16:34.800 --> 00:16:36.800
this card can destroy the opponent's attacking Monster!

00:16:37.100 --> 00:16:39.260
Now be gone, Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:16:39.680 --> 00:16:40.930
N-No way!

00:16:46.610 --> 00:16:47.310
Hope!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:53.110
I'm not done! I'll then use Master Key Beetle to Direct Attack!

00:16:53.860 --> 00:16:55.200
Key Blast!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:03.710
I'll end my turn there.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:07.830
Sure you should be sitting there?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:08.710
What?!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:11.710
You never know when this Sphere Field

00:17:11.710 --> 00:17:15.430
could swallow up everything in this whole city in a heartbeat!

00:17:18.300 --> 00:17:19.140
Crap...!

00:17:19.640 --> 00:17:21.850
He's got three Monsters on his field...

00:17:22.850 --> 00:17:24.890
But on our field...

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:29.860
Without Hope, I can't Rank-Up!

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:30.650
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:35.200
Shingetsu-<i>kun</i>?

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:37.660
Shingetsu!

00:17:38.740 --> 00:17:40.370
You vermin...!

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.290
Yuma-<i>kun</i>, don't give up!

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:46.540
Believe... Believe in your deck!

00:17:48.920 --> 00:17:51.920
<i>That's right... Those cards Shingetsu gave me...</i>

00:17:57.260 --> 00:17:58.010
Yuma?

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:01.560
Here goes! I'm gonna bring it to 'em!

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.560
My turn! Draw!

00:18:08.230 --> 00:18:10.150
Got it!

00:18:13.440 --> 00:18:14.690
Let's win, Astral!

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.990
I Summon V Salamander!

00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:27.250
When V Salamander is Summoned successfully,

00:18:27.620 --> 00:18:30.960
I can Special Summon Aspiring Emperor - Hope from the Graveyard!

00:18:31.210 --> 00:18:34.210
What?! A card to resurrect Hope?!

00:18:35.050 --> 00:18:37.670
Be reborn! Aspiring Emperor - Hope!

00:18:42.720 --> 00:18:47.350
Here goes! I activate the Rank-Up Magic, Limited Barian's Force!

00:18:50.190 --> 00:18:54.190
This card can evolve an Xyz Monster into a Chaos Xyz Monster!

00:18:54.940 --> 00:18:59.110
I use Aspiring Emperor - Hope to rebuild the Overlay Network!

00:19:00.570 --> 00:19:02.200
Chaos Xyz Change!

00:19:04.280 --> 00:19:10.330
Come out, Chaos Number 39! Aspiring Emperor - Hope Ray V!

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.300
Hope Ray V!

00:19:20.800 --> 00:19:23.890
Then I activate V Salamander's effect!

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.970
I equip this Monster on Hope Ray V!

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:28.770
Thunder Cross!

00:19:41.410 --> 00:19:44.410
Here I go! I activate Hope Ray V's effect!

00:19:45.240 --> 00:19:47.040
By detaching one Overlay Unit,

00:19:47.660 --> 00:19:49.790
I can destroy one Monster on the field,

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:53.710
and deal that Monster's Attack Power
 as damage to the opposing player!

00:19:54.840 --> 00:19:58.840
But I have three Monsters on the field!

00:20:00.800 --> 00:20:03.720
Then I activate V Salamander's effect!

00:20:04.550 --> 00:20:09.430
Hope Ray V's effect target will cover every Monster on the field!

00:20:10.060 --> 00:20:13.770
What?! All my Monsters?!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:18.320
You have three 2500 Attack Power Monsters on your field!

00:20:18.860 --> 00:20:21.450
So that's 7500 points of damage!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.820
Go! Hope Ray V!

00:20:25.410 --> 00:20:28.030
V Salamander Inferno!

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:32.410
Impossible! My Monsters...!

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:43.880
Heck yeah! I won!

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.800
You did it, Yuma!

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.010
I'm about to cat.

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.350
<i>V Salamander... What a card...</i>

00:20:57.690 --> 00:21:01.530
How about it?! Did you learn how strong me and Astral are yet?!

00:21:12.000 --> 00:21:12.580
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:14.040 --> 00:21:14.830
Shingetsu!

00:21:16.460 --> 00:21:19.130
Yuma-<i>kun</i>...! It's for the best!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:20.840
Shingetsu!

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.840
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:23.220 --> 00:21:26.550
Did you think I'd <i>actually</i> lose to the likes of you?!

00:21:27.300 --> 00:21:29.930
I'll take this guy instead for now!

00:21:29.930 --> 00:21:30.760
Damn you!

00:21:34.980 --> 00:21:36.140
This is...

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:39.610
If you wanna save this guy, you'll have to ask that card!

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:42.070
Number 66...

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:45.950
That will be the <i>key</i> that will allow us to meet again.

00:21:45.950 --> 00:21:47.070
Yuma-<i>kun</i>!

00:21:47.070 --> 00:21:47.860
Shingetsu!

00:21:49.030 --> 00:21:50.530
Shingetsu!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:56.540
Shit!

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:00.710
Where are you?! Shingetsu! Where'd you go?!

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.340
Shingetsu!

00:22:17.600 --> 00:22:24.480
<i>Does the thought "In any case..." following</i>

00:22:24.900 --> 00:22:32.160
<i>the foreboding premonition tell you to give up?</i>

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:39.750
<i>Do you laugh at your dreams, saying "impossible"?</i>

00:22:39.750 --> 00:22:47.090
<i>You must find it funny that I'm not able to laugh at it, right?</i>

00:22:47.670 --> 00:23:04.070
<i>This song supports me, so I'll do my best for you this time.
 It's my turn to sing now.</i>

00:23:04.070 --> 00:23:08.820
<i>I will vow to you here</i>

00:23:08.820 --> 00:23:19.210
<i>As long as I live, you'll always be my tiny, little friend</i>

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:27.760
<i>I'll erase all those little mistakes of yours</i>

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:32.510
<i>Because I want to become an artist</i>

00:23:34.350 --> 00:23:38.810
<i>Look, I like doing it 'cuz it's fun.</i>

00:23:41.310 --> 00:23:42.980
Shingetsu's been kidnapped by Vector!

00:23:43.610 --> 00:23:44.810
All that's left from the fight

00:23:45.070 --> 00:23:46.780
was the Number that the guy gave us.

00:23:48.230 --> 00:23:50.400
Shingetsu, even if I have to go through hell and high water,

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:52.660
I'm definitely gonna come and save you!

00:23:53.030 --> 00:23:55.330
This fight will certainly be fierce.

00:23:55.530 --> 00:23:56.950
Yuma, something's coming!

00:23:57.290 --> 00:23:59.080
Could this field be...?!

00:23:59.500 --> 00:24:01.370
Heck yeah! Let's set sail, everyone!

00:24:01.960 --> 00:24:03.630
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ZeXal II!

00:24:03.920 --> 00:24:07.000
"Let's Go to the Final Battle!
 Let's Start 'er up, the Emperor's Key Airship!!"

00:24:07.630 --> 00:24:09.260
This is the Barian World?!
